// The attribute cannot be used to ship a set no call can resolve. It exempts the *declarations*
// from the redefinition rule, on the grounds that a rule in the compiler chooses instead -- and
// `concat` is the one name such a rule exists for. For any other name the error simply moves from
// the declaration to the call, where the resolver finds two declarations accepting the arguments
// and says so with the better message: it can list what it is choosing between.
//
// So the attribute buys a prelude name a hand-written rule it already had, and buys program code
// nothing at all.
#[compiler_resolved]
fn pick(xs: variadic int) -> int {
    return 1
}

#[compiler_resolved]
fn pick(xs: variadic int) -> int {
    return 2
}

fn main() {
    print(pick(7))
}
